1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,261
This is for front-desk staff at a hotel.

2
00:00:06,111 --> 00:00:11,082
A guest is standing at the desk, and they need the right answer about
a policy, fast.

3
00:00:11,932 --> 00:00:15,409
It's a simulated hotel group, and the documents are made up.

4
00:00:16,016 --> 00:00:18,149
I'll ask whether a guest can bring their dog.

5
00:00:18,999 --> 00:00:21,431
It searches only this hotel's documents,

6
00:00:22,281 --> 00:00:25,033
and it shows me exactly which passages it used.

7
00:00:25,883 --> 00:00:28,166
There's the source, with the policy text.

8
00:00:28,766 --> 00:00:30,153
So the answer's short.

9
00:00:31,003 --> 00:00:35,013
Dogs up to forty pounds, and a seventy-five dollar fee per stay.

10
00:00:35,863 --> 00:00:39,703
Every fact has a citation, and it won't answer from anywhere else.

11
00:00:40,313 --> 00:00:41,401
Now a follow-up.

12
00:00:42,251 --> 00:00:44,640
I just ask, what about at Mountain Lodge?

13
00:00:45,490 --> 00:00:48,797
It works out I mean the dog question, at the other hotel,

14
00:00:49,647 --> 00:00:51,631
and it shows me how it understood me.

15
00:00:52,481 --> 00:00:54,316
Different hotel, different rule.

16
00:00:54,922 --> 00:00:55,967
Does it hold up?

17
00:00:56,817 --> 00:00:59,911
I test it on fifty-four questions, three runs each,

18
00:01:00,761 --> 00:01:04,153
and it gets ninety-eight to a hundred percent of the answers right,

19
00:01:05,003 --> 00:01:07,392
for under twenty cents per thousand questions.

20
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:09,749
It's live, with no sign-in.

21
00:01:10,599 --> 00:01:12,605
The link's below, and so is the code.
